  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Out-Patient Therapeutic Feeding Pilot Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This pilot project will offer out-patient therapeutic feeding (TF) to severely malnourished children to complement the ongoing provision of supplementary feeding (SF) and in-patient TF being offered by the Catholic Church, MoH and other actors. The pilot will run for three months (October &#x2013; December 2007) from four church clinics (Digsa, Enghela, Feledareb and Mogolo) providing treatment for 120 children. The project will assist severely malnourished children under 5 years old who have been identified as &lt;70% weight-for-height during the SF programme screenings, and who have no medical complications. The pilot project will distribute ready-to-use therapeutic food (Plumpy&#x2019;nut) to these beneficiaries as a take-home ration. The amount requested will cover all the costs of this 3-month pilot project.</narrative>
  </description>
